{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_017Mi8W4R5TPSiEX684vZPeh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/01-030-what-is-mixture-of-experts-moe-how-does-it-improve-efficienc.md`** — Q30: *What is Mixture of Experts (MoE)? How does it improve efficiency?*\n\nKey content in the note:\n- **Concept:** MoE replaces each FFN layer with N expert FFNs + a top-K router, decoupling parameter count from active compute (FLOPs)\n- **Mechanism:** Gating/router → top-K selection → weighted expert outputs → load-balancing auxiliary loss (prevents expert collapse) → expert parallelism in distributed serving\n- **Concrete example:** Mixtral 8×7B (47B total, ~13B active per token, 2/8 experts), comparison table with Switch Transformer and GPT-4\n- **Critical pitfall corrected:** All N experts must be in memory — only *compute* savings, not *memory* savings\n- **Cross-links:** Q2 (transformers), Q34 (memory-bounded inference), Q25 (architecture comparison)\n\n19 items remain in the Next queue before validate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":382,"cache_read_input_tokens":57360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":382,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6455438-4e6c-4915-aa5e-8623ef2dc4b4","uuid":"4afadaf8-819a-417c-8a32-6bad4d11c0b0"}
